
2.2.3. Usage of strcmp() Function
12:49
Write a C program that compares two strings, 
 and 
, entered by the user, using the built-in strcmp() function.



Input Format:

The first line contains the first string 
 (up to 99 characters).
The second line contains the second string 
 (up to 99 characters).


Output Format:

Print "equal" if the strings are the same.
Print "
 is less than 
" if the first string is lexicographically smaller than the second string.
Print "
 is greater than 
" if the first string is lexicographically larger than the second string.


#include <stdio.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
	char str1[100];  // First string
	char str2[100];  // Second string

    int result;
   
    fgets(str1,sizeof(str1),stdin);
    fgets(str2,sizeof(str2),stdin);

	result = strcmp(str1,str2);
	if (result == 0) {
		printf("equal\n");
	} else if (result < 0) {
		printf("str1 is less than str2\n");
	} else {
		printf("str1 is greater than str2\n");
	}
	
	return 0;
}



